From 9add0abff30d2852b545c870b80b349aef5b07e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: __blitzzz <tuanhung303@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 09:51:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/35] fix(compression): harden speculative compression per
 dual blind review
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two independent sol-high blind reviews (core module + integration) found
17 findings; all addressed:

critical: add_done_callback registered under the manager lock deadlocks
when the future completes before registration (reproduced) — callbacks
now register outside the lock (maybe_start + rerun path).

major: wait on manager-published state instead of the future (publication
race); rerun dedup compares full snapshot identity incl. boundary;
candidates carry a compressor-settings fingerprint and are rejected at
install on model/context change; scheduling gates on live cooldown and
anti-thrash state; thresholds respect threshold_tokens_cap and disable
on collapsed small-window watermarks; completed entries are pruned on
every manager access (bounded retention).

minor: bookkeeping keys stripped only at the message top level; _freeze
deep-copies unsupported objects; invalid booleans warn and fall back to
the declared default instead of silently becoming False.

Behavior fixes from the integration review: anti-thrash suppresses only
the forced sync fallback (ready candidates still install), deferred
installs requeue the candidate (restore_candidate), post-tool admission
uses a fresh full-request estimate, _speculative_install_status has
terminal states (rejected/deferred_lock/installed), zero max_age is
honored at install time.
