 iteration-limit summary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

handle_max_iterations() hand-builds api_messages from the live session list
and calls chat.completions.create() directly, bypassing the transport. It
stripped reasoning/finish_reason/tool_name/timestamp/underscore keys but not
display_kind/display_metadata/effect_disposition — fields the main loop
strips per copy (agent/conversation_loop.py) and the transport strips.
TUI/gateway sessions carry them (compaction reference rows marked hidden,
model_switch, skill_invocation, interrupt checkpoints); strict
OpenAI-compatible backends (Fireworks) reject the extras with 400
'Extra inputs are not permitted, field: messages[N].display_kind', so the
max-iterations summary could never succeed on such sessions.

Adds a regression test asserting the request is clean and the source
history is untouched.
---
 agent/chat_completion_helpers.py  | 13 ++++++++++
 tests/run_agent/test_run_agent.py | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 54 insertions(+)

