From a62d97b6737038d94407140f73d58c2e02fb7cac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: __blitzzz <tuanhung303@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 01:36:09 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/35] fix(compression): honor soft-threshold ready candidates
 + live TUI usage after compaction
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RCA (blind sol medium) of three observed issues on the deepseek 524k profile:
the speculative trigger was firing correctly (effective window 524288-64000,
soft = 322201; log source_tokens=322371) — the ~254k display was the TUI gauge
reading a nonexistent agent.messages attribute and falling back to stale
provider occupancy; no post-compaction session.info existed so the status line
froze on the pre-compact value; and a ready speculative candidate was parked
because install policy only claimed at normal/hard pressure, making finished
prep work appear aborted when the tool-wait window closed.

- tui_gateway/server.py: _get_usage now reads the live session history under
  history_lock and estimates with estimate_request_tokens_rough(system_prompt,
  tools) so the gauge matches the admission quantity; the -1 compression
  sentinel reports last_compression_rough_tokens instead of clamping to 0; a
  compacted lifecycle status emits an immediate unthrottled session.info and
  resets the per-session usage throttle.
- agent/turn_context.py: preflight may claim a ready, matching candidate
  nonblocking at or above the speculative soft threshold (allow_soft_ready);
  hard-pressure wait and synchronous fallback are unchanged; no threshold
  arithmetic changed.
- tests: regression coverage for all three RCA findings (gauge estimate,
  post-commit refresh, soft-threshold ready claim).

Verified independently: 511 passed / 1 pre-existing timing flake
(test_write_json_serializes_concurrent_writes).
---
 agent/turn_context.py                         |  16 +--
 package-lock.json                             |  84 +++++----------
