From 461f14e5befab3c47382041a8cc5135167f97e81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: __blitzzz <tuanhung303@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 02:55:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/35] fix(compression): resolve P0/P1 review findings + live
 statusline token estimate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Blind Opus-5 review of 490b1cd86 returned CHANGES REQUESTED (1 P0, 3 P1,
5 P2). This closes the P0/P1 set per the runtime RCA (effective-window
trigger, TUI gauge quantity mismatch, parked ready candidates):

- P0 self-deadlock: _compress_session_history called _get_usage while
  still holding session["history_lock"] (plain non-reentrant Lock) on the
  history_version mismatch branch — a manual compress could wedge the
  session forever. The read now happens outside the lock.
- P1 stale gauge source: _get_usage preferred the pre-turn session
  history snapshot over the live in-turn agent._session_messages, so the
  gauge stayed frozen through tool loops. Live transcript now wins, with
  a locked history fallback for resumed-not-yet-run sessions; the whole
  estimate block is skipped on the -1 compression sentinel.
- P1 monotonic floor: the rough live estimate previously overwrote the
  last real provider occupancy unconditionally, letting the gauge
  under-report pressure. Now max(last_prompt, live_estimate).
- P1 codex pre-compaction figure: codex_runtime.py stored the ADMISSION
  estimate (approx_tokens) into last_compression_rough_tokens, so the new
  post-commit gauge emit snapped back to the full pre-compact context on
  the Codex app-server route. Now stores the turn's reported post-boundary
  input tokens (inputTokens + cachedInputTokens), else 0.
- P2-5 anti-thrash breaker noted as follow-up (soft claim does not consult
  _automatic_compression_blocked).
- P2-6 commit_at_soft_threshold config gate left for a config-surface
  change; not folded here to keep the fix slice reviewable.
- P2-7/P2-8 also folded: _get_usage session scan now under _sessions_lock
  (callers pass the session they already hold), and the lock+copy work is
  hoisted behind the use_live_estimate guard.

Statusline cosmetics while compacting:
- Backend surfaces the speculative estimate as a structured payload token
  (status.update.tokens) parsed from the existing "~322,371 tokens" text.
- TUI shows "optimizing ctx ~322k" in muted/dim italic instead of the
  dots once an estimate exists; dots remain the pre-estimate fallback.
- ui-store/interfaces/gatewayTypes carry speculativeCompressionTokens end
  to end; appChrome test extended; vitest, tsc, eslint clean.

Also bundles the concurrent TPS-meter and per-model service-tier work that
was already in the working tree (user confirmed both complete): live TPS
readout in the status bar and resolve_service_tier_config per-model
overrides with tests.

Pre-existing unrelated failures verified on clean HEAD (not introduced):
subscriptionOverlay.test.tsx (19) and ink-backpressure.test.ts (1) —
both repro without this diff.
